<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Nepalese War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a>–<a href="/years/1816">1816</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Gurkha War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Nepalese War was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. It ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-sugauli">Treaty of Sugauli</a>, by which Nepal gave up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumaon">Kumaon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garhwal">Garhwal</a> and the hill country between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> and the Kali. The British restored many small hill states that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurkhas">Gorkhas</a> had conquered, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simla-hill-states">Simla Hill States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-nepalese-war.jpg" alt="Anglo-Nepalese War" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Henry Thompson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Death_of_Rollo_Gillespie_(Cassell%27s_illustrated_history_of_India).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
